{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Keep application data under /srv/data recoverable through filesystem snapshots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Root-only, legacy-compatible snapshot and restore utilities were installed, a baseline snapshot was created, and direct comparisons showed that it matched /srv/data, including hashes, modes, ownership, symlink target, and hard-link topology. Snapshot creation also succeeded after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5204cf0288a4612","cmd-78ba5143bf49473c","cmd-7f526ac80419457f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"After modifying /srv/data, restore the exact content captured by the earlier snapshot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor directly demonstrated changed, deleted, and added data, then restored the earlier snapshot. The final checksum comparison was empty, original hashes and metadata returned, the added file disappeared, the deleted file and original symlink returned, and hard-link topology was preserved.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f0768ce4da647c3","cmd-cb4a36170b294d51"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation used the platform's existing rsync 2.6.9 and cron facilities. Ubuntu 7.10 with kernel 2.6.22-14-generic remained present after configuration and reboot, matching the baseline kernel observation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a20ce88300344f35","cmd-58833a7901614021","cmd-7f526ac80419457f","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Tool installation, test-data creation, deliberate data divergence, restoration, and retained verification snapshots all had clear roles in implementing or proving the required recovery flow. The failed ACL-preserving snapshot attempt was cleaned by its trap, and the bounded temporary rsync compatibility tests directly identified the incompatible -A option; their temporary artifacts were absent in the final lifecycle inventory. Package health and socket inventory showed no executor-caused degradation. The mandatory restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot ID, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart snapshot operation; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5204cf0288a4612","cmd-5cb149a7a9354d1c","cmd-4d7bedd5491d499d","cmd-3840c8b07539471c","cmd-78ba5143bf49473c","cmd-4f0768ce4da647c3","cmd-cb4a36170b294d51","cmd-49d981cd50754e1b","cmd-ab3bafcac8124e23","cmd-f798b213878648c0","cmd-7f526ac80419457f","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct snapshot, divergence, rollback, exact-comparison, legacy-platform, and reboot-recovery evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete and coherent with the independent lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The legacy node does not support the lifecycle collector's systemd failed-unit check; applicable cron and SSH processes were instead checked directly after reboot.","Extended ACLs and xattrs were not part of the final rsync mode or explicitly validated. The demonstrated dataset's contents, ordinary metadata, symlink, and hard-link topology were validated directly."]}
